//Composition
Composition means one class contains an object of another class as a member.

It represents a strong "has-a" relationship.

Example:

class Engine {
public:
    void start() {
        cout << "Engine started";
    }
};

class Car {
private:
    Engine engine;

public:
    void startCar() {
        engine.start();
    }
};

Here:

Car has an Engine
engine is a data member of Car
Car c;
c.startCar();
Important idea

The Engine object is part of the Car.

Car
 └── Engine

If the Car object is destroyed, its contained Engine object is also destroyed.

Inheritance vs Composition

Inheritance:

Dog is an Animal

Composition:

Car has an Engine

Simple definition:

Composition = a class contains an object of another class as a member, creating a strong has-a relationship.